In Slash'EM, Hobbits are permitted to be Archaeologists, Healers,
Monks, Priests, Rangers, Tourists, Wizards, and a few other classes
which don't exist in vanilla Nethack.  Actually they probably
shouldn't be allowed to be Monks, since hobbits tend to eat a lot and
monks do not.  I suppose you ruled out Healers and Wizards because
Hobbits tend not to use magic?

If you want to allow Hobbit Rogues, you could permit Rogues to be
neutral as well as chaotic (according to the Baldur's Gate II manual,
thieves are permitted to be any alignment except Lawful Good).  Or you
could permit Hobbits to be of any alignment, though that is currently
the one distinguishing feature of humans.  Or you could rationalise
forbidding them to be lawful by saying that although the vast majority
of hobbits are lawful, a lawful hobbit would *never* go adventuring
because the other hobbits would strongly disapprove - so any hobbit
that can violate the community norms to that extent must be neutral or
chaotic.
